mpvpaper: one exit, from the render loop

Stopped with a signal, mpvpaper started a thread from its signal handler
(not something a handler may do: it can wait for ever on a lock the
interrupted thread holds), and that thread destroyed mpv while the mpv event
thread was still waiting inside it; the event thread, seeing mpv's shutdown
event, then ran the same exit a second time beside the first: mpv freed
twice and two exit() at once. On totoro that was a segfault in exit() at
about every other stop (8 core dumps in a week), and once a player that
never ended, which held nixbook-shell's restart for systemd's 90 seconds.

Now the handler only notes the request, wakes the render loop and sets a
3 second alarm; the render loop leaves from its own thread (nothing draws
meanwhile); the exit runs once, a second caller waits; the event thread is
out of mpv before mpv is destroyed; and the process ends with _exit(), not
exit(), whose handlers ran beside the threads still alive.

